p.src:
The metric is compatible with the derivative operator: $\nabla_r g_{mn}=0,
\qquad
\nabla_r g^{mn}=0.$ For a covector $V_s$, the covariant derivative is $\nabla_r V_s
=
\partial_r V_s-\Gamma^p{}_{rs}V_p.$ The connection coefficients are $\Gamma^p{}_{rs}
=
\frac{1}{2}g^{pn}
\left(
\partial_s g_{nr}
+\partial_r g_{ns}
-\partial_n g_{rs}
\right).$ Several indices are corrected while this expression is written on the board. Equation [eq:l4-christoffel] is the completed relation. It is symmetric in $r$ and $s$, as expected for the torsion-free Levi-Civita connection.

