p.src:
Now calculate the one required connection coefficient. The metric is diagonal and independent of $t$, so $\begin{aligned}\Gamma^y{}_{tt}
&=
\frac{1}{2}g^{yy}
\left(
\partial_tg_{yt}
+\partial_tg_{ty}
-\partial_yg_{tt}
\right)\\
&=
-\frac{1}{2}\partial_yg_{tt},
\end{aligned}$ because $g^{yy}=1$ in the lecture’s mostly-plus tensor convention.

